      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.17,
          "end": 6.023,
          "en": "So it's finally time to start taking pictures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.92,
          "end": 10.48,
          "en": "And for that, I wanna add a new component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.48,
          "end": 11.93,
          "en": "which I will name ImagePicker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 17.83,
          "en": "because taking pictures is actually a process that consists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.83,
          "end": 19.62,
          "en": "of multiple steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.62,
          "end": 22.06,
          "en": "We will have to open the camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.06,
          "end": 25.09,
          "en": "and show a button that allows the user to do so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.09,
          "end": 27.04,
          "en": "But then I also wanna show a preview",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.04,
          "end": 28.37,
          "en": "of the image and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.37,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "of course we will have a UI that has multiple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 35.8,
          "en": "elements and also some logic attached to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.8,
          "end": 39.16,
          "en": "But before we get started working on that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.16,
          "end": 43.34,
          "en": "let's understand how we can actually use the device camera.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.34,
          "end": 47.4,
          "en": "And here ReactNative makes it quite straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.4,
          "end": 50.19,
          "en": "and easy for us to use native device features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 53.67,
          "en": "like this especially when we're using Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.67,
          "end": 55.25,
          "en": "We are using Expo here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.25,
          "end": 58.18,
          "en": "So we can for example, search for Expo Camera.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.18,
          "end": 60.59,
          "en": "And that is generally a good approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.59,
          "end": 63.28,
          "en": "If you, for example wanna use the user location",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.28,
          "end": 66.04,
          "en": "you could search Expo Location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.04,
          "end": 71.03999999999999,
          "en": "If you want to, let's say store data on the device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.24,
          "end": 74.5,
          "en": "you could search for Expo Storage and you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.5,
          "end": 77.75,
          "en": "would find different packages that might help you with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.75,
          "end": 80.6,
          "en": "Now here it's Expo Camera, and we can go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.6,
          "end": 83.90299999999999,
          "en": "to the Expo Documentation to learn more about this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.74,
          "end": 88.37,
          "en": "Now Expo Camera actually is a package that does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.37,
          "end": 91.25,
          "en": "not just open the device camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.25,
          "end": 96.00999999999999,
          "en": "but instead it allows you to customize the camera screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.00999999999999,
          "end": 98.93,
          "en": "You can control auto focus, zoom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.93,
          "end": 102.37,
          "en": "You can build your own camera based UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.37,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "and for some apps where the camera plays a major role",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "and is not just about taking some photo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.56,
          "end": 112.88,
          "en": "that of course can be a very important feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.88,
          "end": 116.81,
          "en": "But for our app here, this would actually be overkill",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.81,
          "end": 120.72,
          "en": "because I don't really need to configure the camera screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 124.37,
          "en": "Instead I just want to use some default camera screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.37,
          "end": 127.45,
          "en": "that simply allows me to take an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.45,
          "end": 129.02,
          "en": "Nonetheless, it's worth noting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.02,
          "end": 130.99,
          "en": "that you have packages like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.99,
          "end": 134.351,
          "en": "And what's really important is that whenever you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.351,
          "end": 138.22,
          "en": "are about to use a package like this definitely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.22,
          "end": 140.87,
          "en": "have a look at the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.87,
          "end": 144.82,
          "en": "like this documentation page here for the camera.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.82,
          "end": 148.05,
          "en": "There you learn where this package can and be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.05,
          "end": 151.3,
          "en": "how it works and how you can install and configure it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.3,
          "end": 153.43200000000002,
          "en": "And it's really important that you go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.43200000000002,
          "end": 156,
          "en": "through these instructions to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156,
          "end": 158.03300000000002,
          "en": "that you use the package correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.9,
          "end": 161.11,
          "en": "However, as I said, the camera package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.11,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "the Expo Camera Package is a bit overkill",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 166.55,
          "en": "for what we're going to build here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.55,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "Instead, another package which is more useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 172.73,
          "en": "to us here is the ImagePicker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.73,
          "end": 175.93,
          "en": "because this is a package that allows us to open",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.93,
          "end": 180.26,
          "en": "the on device photos or on the launch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.26,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "the camera both as possible with this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 186.55,
          "en": "And therefore that's the package we're going to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.55,
          "end": 188.73,
          "en": "And we're going to follow the installation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.73,
          "end": 190.61,
          "en": "Instructions mentioned here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.61,
          "end": 192.74,
          "en": "which in this case is this one command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.74,
          "end": 195.48,
          "en": "So I will open a new Terminal window",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.48,
          "end": 199.453,
          "en": "and run expo install, expo-image-picker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.574,
          "end": 202.36,
          "en": "This will install this package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.36,
          "end": 204.833,
          "en": "into this project so that we can use it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.05,
          "end": 208.07,
          "en": "Now once that was done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.07,
          "end": 209.99,
          "en": "we can close this extra Terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.99,
          "end": 210.91,
          "en": "And then as mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.91,
          "end": 215.13,
          "en": "we can learn how to use it here in this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.13,
          "end": 217.52,
          "en": "And therefore example is some configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.52,
          "end": 221.28,
          "en": "that we should set up to manage permissions correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 224.12,
          "en": "Because that is an important topic when working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.12,
          "end": 227.473,
          "en": "with Native Device Features permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.36,
          "end": 231.68,
          "en": "Many Native Device Features need permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.68,
          "end": 234.2,
          "en": "to be granted by the device user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.2,
          "end": 237.15,
          "en": "For example, if your app wants to use the camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.15,
          "end": 238.9,
          "en": "a user needs to give his",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.9,
          "end": 241.663,
          "en": "or her permission for your app to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.73,
          "end": 245.42,
          "en": "Now you must register permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.42,
          "end": 248.33,
          "en": "your app will use ahead of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.33,
          "end": 251.24,
          "en": "And most packages exposed by Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.24,
          "end": 254.57,
          "en": "make registering such permissions quite easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.57,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "and straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 259.44,
          "en": "By the way you find different instructions here also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.44,
          "end": 262.46,
          "en": "for cases where you would not be using Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.46,
          "end": 265.34,
          "en": "and you still want to use this package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.34,
          "end": 269.67,
          "en": "But here for us what is important is actually this entry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.67,
          "end": 272.733,
          "en": "which should be added to the app.Json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 273.96,
          "end": 278.02,
          "en": "We should add this plugins entry here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.02,
          "end": 281.09000000000003,
          "en": "into our app.Json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.09000000000003,
          "end": 283.31,
          "en": "So here, maybe at the bottom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 283.31,
          "end": 285.76,
          "en": "we should at this plugins note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 285.76,
          "end": 287.26,
          "en": "which holds this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.26,
          "end": 290.303,
          "en": "which in the end sets the permissions we wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 292.77,
          "end": 295.95,
          "en": "Now we learn which permissions can be configured here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 295.95,
          "end": 298.46,
          "en": "And in my case, I wanna open the camera.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.46,
          "end": 301.01,
          "en": "So I'm not interested in the photos permission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 301.01,
          "end": 304.323,
          "en": "Instead, I'm interested in the Camerapermission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 304.323,
          "end": 307.28,
          "en": "Therefore, I will change this node here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 307.28,
          "end": 309.03,
          "en": "to CameraPermission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.03,
          "end": 310.9,
          "en": "And then you can enter some texts here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.9,
          "end": 312.97,
          "en": "which will be shown on iOS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.97,
          "end": 316.63,
          "en": "when the user is prompted to grant the permission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 316.63,
          "end": 319.62,
          "en": "So here you can explain why you need the permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.62,
          "end": 322.173,
          "en": "to convince the user to grant it to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 323.09,
          "end": 328.09,
          "en": "So here we could therefore say something like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 328.127,
          "end": 332.1,
          "en": "\"The app needs access to your camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.1,
          "end": 337.1,
          "en": "in order to take photos of your favorite places.\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 339.68,
          "end": 341.23,
          "en": "Something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 341.23,
          "end": 343.95,
          "en": "So this needs to be added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 343.95,
          "end": 346.15,
          "en": "And we know that this must be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.15,
          "end": 348.26,
          "en": "because the documentation page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 348.26,
          "end": 350.823,
          "en": "of this plugin tells us to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.68,
          "end": 354.88,
          "en": "Not all packages need this kind of configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.88,
          "end": 356.39,
          "en": "but the ImagePicker does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.39,
          "end": 358.83,
          "en": "And That's why it's important to read the official",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 358.83,
          "end": 359.763,
          "en": "documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.12,
          "end": 364.03,
          "en": "Now, with that, we got this configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 364.03,
          "end": 365.77,
          "en": "and now in the next lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
